.TH MEMREDUCT 1 "2026" "memreduct 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memreduct \- real-time memory monitoring and cleaning for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memreduct
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memreduct
is a lightweight real-time memory management application to monitor and
clean system memory. It is the Linux port of Mem Reduct for Windows.
.PP
It reads system memory from
.I /proc/meminfo ,
pressure stall information from
.IR /proc/pressure/ ,
VM counters from
.I /proc/vmstat
and optional ZRAM and cgroup v2 statistics from sysfs and cgroupfs.
It cleans memory through documented kernel interfaces including
.IR /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches ,
.I /proc/sys/vm/compact_memory
and, optionally, swap reload. Cleaning requires root privileges;
monitoring does not.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show current memory usage (default command).
.TP
.B stats
Show a detailed memory breakdown, PSI pressure, ZRAM compression,
VM reclaim counters, cgroup v2 usage and top memory consumers.
.TP
.B clean
Clean memory immediately.
.TP
.B top
Show the processes using the most memory (resident set size).
.TP
.B monitor
Interactive full-screen live monitor with usage history graph, memory
pressure and top memory consumers. Press
.B c
to clean memory,
.B q
to quit.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the auto-clean daemon in the foreground (used by the systemd unit).
It can clean when physical memory usage or PSI memory pressure reaches a
configured threshold, and/or every configured interval.
.SH CLEANING AREAS
.TP
.B \-\-pagecache
Drop clean page cache.
.TP
.B \-\-dentries
Drop dentry and inode slab caches.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Compact fragmented physical memory.
.TP
.B \-\-modified-cache
Run the system-wide
.B sync
operation to write dirty file-backed pages so they can become reclaimable.
This does not discard application memory, but it can initiate disk writes.
.TP
.B \-\-swap
Move swapped pages back into RAM by running
.B swapoff \-a
followed by
.BR "swapon \-a" .
Skipped when the swapped data would not fit into available RAM.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Enable all supported cleaning areas, including swap reload. Use swap reload
with care; it is disabled in the default configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-t, \-\-threshold " pct
Auto-clean when physical memory usage reaches
.I pct
percent (daemon mode, 0 disables).
.TP
.BI "\-p, \-\-pressure " pct
Auto-clean when the selected PSI memory
.B avg10
reaches
.I pct
percent (daemon mode, 0 disables; requires PSI support).
.TP
.BI "\-\-pressure-type " mode
Select the PSI memory metric for automatic cleaning:
.B some
(default, at least one task stalled) or
.B full
(all non-idle tasks stalled simultaneously).
.TP
.BI "\-n, \-\-interval " min
Auto-clean every
.I min
minutes (daemon mode, 0 disables).
.TP
.BI "\-i, \-\-refresh " sec
Refresh period for monitor mode / poll period for daemon mode.
.TP
.BI "\-l, \-\-limit " n
Number of processes to show for the
.B top
command (default 10).
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON output for the
.B status ,
.B stats
and
.B top
commands. Optional kernel metrics are represented by availability flags and
zero-valued counters when the underlying interface is unavailable.
.TP
.BI "\-c, \-\-config " file
Use an alternative configuration file.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Disable desktop notifications.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version.
.SH METRICS
.TP
.B PSI
Reads memory, CPU and I/O pressure averages and cumulative stall time.
Memory PSI provides both
.B some
and
.B full
metrics.
.TP
.B ZRAM
Aggregates device statistics from
.I /sys/block/zram*/mm_stat
when ZRAM devices are present.
.TP
.B VM STATISTICS
Reads page faults, major faults, swap I/O, reclaim, compaction and OOM-kill
counters from
.IR /proc/vmstat .
Counters are cumulative since boot.
.TP
.B CGROUP V2
Reports the cgroup containing the current process when the unified hierarchy
is mounted at
.IR /sys/fs/cgroup .
This is especially useful when the process runs in a systemd unit or container.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/memreduct.conf
System-wide configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/memreduct/memreduct.conf
Per-user configuration (overrides the system-wide file).
.SH SIGNALS
The daemon reloads its configuration on
.B SIGHUP
and exits cleanly on
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGTERM .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Show detailed memory statistics:
.B memreduct stats
.TP
Clean cache and modified file-backed pages:
.B sudo memreduct clean --pagecache --modified-cache
.TP
Clean everything, including swap reload:
.B sudo memreduct clean --all
.TP
Watch memory live and clean on demand:
.B sudo memreduct monitor
.TP
Run the daemon, cleaning at 85% usage:
.B sudo memreduct daemon --threshold 85
.TP
Run the daemon when memory PSI some avg10 reaches 10%:
.B sudo memreduct daemon --pressure 10
.TP
Run the daemon only when memory PSI full avg10 reaches 5%:
.B sudo memreduct daemon --pressure 5 --pressure-type full
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR free (1),
.BR sync (2),
.BR proc (5),
.BR zramctl (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Original Windows version by Henry++ <https://github.com/henrypp/memreduct>.
